examples.solution_text:
The equations of motion are
$\begin{align*}\dot{x}&=12\sqrt{3},&x&=12\sqrt{3}t,\\\dot{y}&=12-10t,&y&=12t-5t^2.\end{align*}$
(a) At greatest height, $\dot{y}=0$.
$\begin{align*}0&=12-10t\\t&=1.2\text{ s}.\end{align*}$
(b) Substitute this time into $y(t)$.
$\begin{align*}y(1.2)&=12(1.2)-5(1.2)^2\\&=7.2\text{ m}.\end{align*}$
(c) At landing, $y=0$.
$\begin{align*}0&=12t-5t^2\\0&=t(12-5t)\\t&=0\text{ or }2.4.\end{align*}$
The time of flight is $2.4\text{ s}$; $t=0$ is the launch.
(d) Substitute the landing time into $x(t)$.
$\begin{align*}x(2.4)&=12\sqrt{3}(2.4)\\&=28.8\sqrt{3}\text{ m}.\end{align*}$
(e) At landing,
$\begin{align*}\dot{x}(2.4)&=12\sqrt{3}\\\dot{y}(2.4)&=12-10(2.4)\\&=-12.\end{align*}$
$\begin{align*}\text{Speed}&=\sqrt{(12\sqrt{3})^2+(-12)^2}\\&=24\text{ m/s},\\\theta&=\tan^{-1}\left(\frac{12}{12\sqrt{3}}\right)\\&=30^\circ.\end{align*}$
The ball lands at $24\text{ m/s}$ at $30^\circ$ below the horizontal.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.12cm,y=0.22cm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont},draw=black,text=black]
\draw[->] (-2,0)--(54,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-1)--(0,10) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,domain=0:49.883,samples=80,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{\x/1.7320508-5*(\x/20.78461)*(\x/20.78461)});
\draw[dashed] (24.9415,0)--(24.9415,7.2);
\fill (24.9415,7.2) circle (1.5pt);
\node[above] at (24.9415,7.2) {$H=7.2\text{ m},\ \dot{y}=0$};
\draw[<->] (0,-2)--(49.883,-2) node[midway,below] {$R=28.8\sqrt{3}\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.question_text:
A ball rolls horizontally off a $45\text{ m}$ cliff at $16\text{ m/s}$. Take the launch point as the origin and $g=10\text{ m/s}^2$. Find (a) the time of flight, (b) the horizontal distance from the base to its landing point and (c) its impact speed and direction, to $1$ decimal place where necessary.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont},draw=black,text=black]
\draw (-1,3)--(0,3)--(0,0)--(5,0);
\fill (0,3) circle (1.5pt);
\node[above left] at (0,3) {$O$};
\draw[->,thick] (0,3)--(2,3) node[midway,above] {$16\text{ m/s}$};
\draw[<->] (-0.6,0)--(-0.6,3) node[midway,left] {$45\text{ m}$};
\node[below right] at (0,0) {Ground};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A stone is thrown from a $30\text{ m}$ tower at $20\text{ m/s}$ at $30^\circ$ below the horizontal. Take the launch point as the origin and $g=10\text{ m/s}^2$. Find the time it takes to reach the ground.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont},draw=black,text=black]
\draw (-1,3)--(0,3)--(0,0)--(5,0);
\draw[dashed] (0,3)--(2.7,3);
\draw[->,thick] (0,3)--(2.165,1.75) node[right] {$20\text{ m/s}$};
\draw (0.7,3) arc[start angle=0,end angle=-30,radius=0.7];
\node at (1.15,2.7) {$30^\circ$};
\node[above left] at (0,3) {$O$};
\draw[<->] (-0.6,0)--(-0.6,3) node[midway,left] {$30\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
